var resourceFreecellTxt = &fyne.StaticResource{
	StaticName: "freecell.txt",
	StaticContent: []byte(
		"### (Freecell) Patience / Solitaire\r\nObjective is to gather consecutive cards from Ace to King of the same suit.\r\nThe board consists of three areas - Card Columns, Free, and Foundation.\r\n- Card Columns (8 card columns) are all of the cards not in the Free or Foundation areas.\r\n- The Free area (4 cells) is a temporary \"parking\" spot to free up buried\r\ncards in the Card Columns.\r\n- The Foundation piles (4 suits - ♣,♦,♥,♠, each in ascending rank).\r\nThe game is \"won\" when all 4 suits are complete.\r\nA \"sequence\" is 1 or more cards in descending rank and alternating colors - ♣clubs and ♠spades are black, ♦diamonds and ♥hearts are red.\r\n### Gameplay\r\n- Clicking the \"DEAL\" button presents a new board.\r\n- All 52 cards are dealt face up. 7 in the first 4 columns and 6 in the last 4 columns.\r\n- Clicking the \"UNDO\" button reverses the last valid move.\r\n- Setting the \"Hints\" to \"on\" provides a useful hint for the next move.\r\n- Cards are moved via drag-and-drop:\r\nMove the mouse to the card to select a card or sequence.\r\nPressing the Primary mouse button selects the cell.\r\nSelecting the first card of a sequence selects the entire sequence.\r\nMoving the mouse while holding the button down drags the card's icon (i.e. 10♦).\r\nWhile moving, any valid destination cell is highlighted and an invalid destination is dimmed. Locations outside of the card areas are not tracked.\r\nReleasing the mouse button ends the move. If it in a valid location, the card(s) are removed from the original location and placed on the destination.\r\n### Specific Rules\r\n- Card Columns must be built with descending rank and alternating colors.\r\n- Foundations are built ascending by the common suit.\r\n- Any Free card or top card of any card column may be moved to build on another column, moved to an empty Free card, or its Foundation.\r\n- Any sequence from a card column may be moved to another card column whose top has a rank one greater and opposite color as the rank/color of that sequence.\r\n- Only a single card may be moved from the top of a Card Column to an empty Free or Foundation cell.\r\n- Only a King (or King sequence) may be placed on an empty Card Column.\r\n\r\nMIT License - 2026\r\n"),
}
